-- title:
--   Frob_q² = q² on the monodromy toric part of J₀(Nq)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ and $q$ be nonzero natural numbers with $q$ prime and $q \nmid N$. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll (N * q)`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll.html#L8), i.e. for every prime $\ell$ the package `HeckeInputsAlong` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ holds at level $N q$ and $\ell$ (integrality of the two Hecke correspondences, existence of principal divisors for the base-changed modular function field, finiteness of the $\alpha$-map, and the fundamental identity together with the norm formula), and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar (N * q)`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L25), i.e. the operators `heckeOperatorBar (N * q) ℓ` commute pairwise on $J =$ `JZero (N * q)`, the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field at level $Nq$ base-changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ belongs to the nonunits of $A$, and let $\mathrm{frob}$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is a Frobenius at $A$ for $q$: it lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acts on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^q$. Then, for the `HeckeAlg`-module structure `heckeModuleBar (N * q)` on $J$ (the action of $\mathbb{Z}[T_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ through the commuting Hecke operators), every element $x$ of the `HeckeAlg`-submodule of $J$ spanned by the differences $\sigma \bullet y - y$, with $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ and $y \in J$ annihilated by some $m > 0$ coprime to $q$, satisfies $\mathrm{frob} \bullet (\mathrm{frob} \bullet x) = q^2 \cdot x$.
--
--   This is the Frobenius clause of Ribet's local analysis of $J_0(Nq)$ at the prime $q$ of multiplicative reduction: on the toric part the square of Frobenius acts by $q^2$, reflecting that the torus of the special fibre is split over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. Here the toric part is taken in the explicit form of the monodromy toric part, the Hecke submodule generated by inertia-monodromy differences on prime-to-$q$ torsion; the statement feeds the Galois-theoretic input to the level-lowering step and to the construction of lower-level torsion in the Frey curve argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_toricFrobeniusSq_toricMonodromyPart_jZero.lean

